{title: Mack the Knife}
{subtitle: arr. Tony Guerrero}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 160}

# Bars separated by |. Several chords in one bar = split evenly.
# %  repeat the previous bar
# |: :|  repeat marks      {ending: n}  first/second endings
# X!  force the root INTO the voicing (as played)   X~  force it rootless
#     (default is rootless-preferred; the marker overrides per chord)

# The tonic 6 chord is comped with its root here, the way it sits on the
# recording -- hence Bb6! (and C6! in the shout, the same chord up a tone).
{section: A - a la Freddie Green}
| Bb6! | % | % | % |

{section: B - head}
|: Bb6! | % | Cm7 | % |
| F7 | % | Bb6! | % |
| Dm7 | Dbo7 | Cm7 | F7 |
| Cm7 | F7 | Bb6! | % :|

{section: G - shout, up a tone}
| C6! | % | Dm7 | G7 |
| Dm7 | G7 | C6! | % |
| Em7 | Ebo7 | Dm7 | G13 |

{section: chromatic run}
| Dm9 | Dm9 | Ebm9 | Em9 |
| Fm9 | Fm9 | Em9 | Ebm9 |
| Dm9 | G13 | C6 | % |
